00:52:45,331 --> 00:52:46,032
Rym: Rebecca Dunn.

610
00:52:46,112 --> 00:52:46,853
Rym: Sam Erickson.

611
00:52:47,234 --> 00:52:48,035
Rym: Shervin von Horrell.

612
00:52:48,135 --> 00:52:51,120
Rym: And a ton of people whose names I am not going to say.

613
00:52:51,461 --> 00:52:56,277
Rym: I was trying to think of what to leave you with tonight, and I think an appropriate choice would be...

614
00:52:57,260 --> 00:53:00,265
Media: I'm sorry, but I don't want to be an emperor.

615
00:53:00,686 --> 00:53:01,567
Media: That's not my business.

616
00:53:02,869 --> 00:53:04,572
Media: I don't want to rule or conquer anyone.

617
00:53:05,273 --> 00:53:06,776
Media: I should like to help everyone if possible.

618
00:53:07,176 --> 00:53:09,500
Media: Jew, Gentile, black man, white.

619
00:53:10,500 --> 00:53:11,745
Media: We all want to help one another.

620
00:53:12,026 --> 00:53:13,190
Media: Human beings are like that.

621
00:53:13,892 --> 00:53:16,140
Media: We want to live by each other's happiness, not by each other's misery.

622
00:53:17,061 --> 00:53:18,766
Media: We don't want to hate and despise one another.

623
00:53:19,488 --> 00:53:23,900
Media: In this world there's room for everyone, and the good earth is rich and can provide for everyone.

624
00:53:24,500 --> 00:53:28,507
Media: The way of life can be free and beautiful, but we have lost the way.

625
00:53:29,529 --> 00:53:36,340
Media: Greed has poisoned men's souls, has barricaded the world with hate, has goose-stepped us into misery and bloodshed.

626
00:53:37,222 --> 00:53:39,907
Media: We have developed speed, but we have shut ourselves in.

627
00:53:40,588 --> 00:53:42,832
Media: Machinery that gives abundance has left us in want.

628
00:53:43,494 --> 00:53:46,680
Media: Our knowledge has made us cynical, our cleverness hard and unkind.

629
00:53:47,380 --> 00:53:49,465
Media: We think too much and feel too little.

630
00:53:50,167 --> 00:53:52,332
Media: More than machinery, we need humanity.

631
00:53:52,813 --> 00:53:55,620
Media: More than cleverness, we need kindness and gentleness.

632
00:53:56,320 --> 00:53:59,670
Media: Without these qualities, life will be violent and all will be lost.

633
00:54:00,453 --> 00:54:02,740
Media: The aeroplane and the radio have brought us closer together.

634
00:54:03,101 --> 00:54:08,940
Media: The very nature of these inventions cries out for the goodness in men, cries out for universal brotherhood, for the unity of us all.

635
00:54:09,600 --> 00:54:19,780
Media: Even now my voice is reaching millions throughout the world, millions of despairing men, women and little children, victims of a system that makes men torture and imprison innocent people.

636
00:54:20,700 --> 00:54:23,446
Media: To those who can hear me, I say, do not despair.

637
00:54:23,466 --> 00:54:30,120
Media: The misery that is now upon us is but the passing of greed, the bitterness of men who fear the way of human progress.

638
00:54:30,821 --> 00:54:37,214
Media: The hate of men will pass and dictators die and the power they took from the people will return to the people.

639
00:54:37,574 --> 00:54:40,480
Media: And so long as men die, liberty will never perish.

640
00:54:42,580 --> 00:54:44,603
Rym: Soldiers, don't give yourselves to brutes.

641
00:54:45,224 --> 00:54:54,640
Scott: Men who despise you, enslave you, who regiment your lives, tell you what to do, what to think and what to feel, who drill you, diet you, treat you like cattle, use you as cannon fodder.

642
00:54:55,221 --> 00:55:00,792
Rym: Don't give yourselves to these unnatural men, machine men with machine minds and machine hearts.

643
00:55:01,313 --> 00:55:04,380
Scott: You are not machines, you are not cattle, you are men.

644
00:55:05,060 --> 00:55:06,866
Media: You have the love of humanity in your hearts.

645
00:55:07,227 --> 00:55:08,973
Media: You don't hate, only the unloved.

646
00:55:09,013 --> 00:55:11,020
Media: hate, the unloved and the unnatural.

647
00:55:11,560 --> 00:55:14,546
Media: Soldiers, don't fight for slavery, fight for liberty.

648
00:55:14,927 --> 00:55:16,129
Media: In the seventeenth chapter of St.

649
00:55:16,149 --> 00:55:16,289
Media: Luke.

650
00:55:16,309 --> 00:55:21,780
Rym: it is written, the kingdom of God is within man, not one man nor a group of men, but in all men, in you.

651
00:55:22,181 --> 00:55:26,909
Scott: You the people have the power, the power to create machines, the power to create happiness.

652
00:55:27,150 --> 00:55:32,500
Scott: You the people have the power to make this life free and beautiful, to make this life a wonderful adventure.

653
00:55:32,960 --> 00:55:45,180
Scott: Then in the name of democracy, let us use that power, let us all unite, let us fight for a new world, a decent world that will give men a chance to work, that will give youth a future and old age a security.

654
00:55:45,641 --> 00:55:55,520
Media: By the promise of these things, brutes have risen to power, but they lie, they do not fulfill that promise, they never will, dictators free themselves, but they enslave the people.

655
00:55:56,060 --> 00:56:06,180
Media: Now let us fight to fulfill that promise, let us fight to free the world, to do away with national barriers, to do away with greed, with hate and intolerance.

656
00:56:06,920 --> 00:56:12,880
Scott: Let us fight for a world of reason, a world where science and progress will lead to all men's happiness.

657
00:56:13,744 --> 00:56:17,200
Media: Soldiers in the name of democracy, let us all unite!

